{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":1148356,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,28]],"date-time":"2026-02-28T09:39:01Z","timestamp":1772271541397,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"PeerJ","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.660\/supp-2","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,8,5]],"date-time":"2021-08-05T03:53:38Z","timestamp":1628135618000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Supplemental Information 2: The text based review dataset taken from Amazon, Imdb, and Yelp websites"],"prefix":"10.7717","member":"4443","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2021,8,5]],"date-time":"2021-08-05T03:53:42Z","timestamp":1628135622000},"score":45.909466,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/peerj.com\/articles\/cs-660\/supp-2"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7717\/peerj-cs.660\/supp-2","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.660","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,28]],"date-time":"2026-02-28T09:31:43Z","timestamp":1772271103375,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"PeerJ","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.2011\/supp-1","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,4,30]],"date-time":"2024-04-30T04:34:13Z","timestamp":1714451653000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Supplemental Information 1: The YELP-5 dataset is a sentiment classification task dataset used for sentiment analysis. It comprises user reviews sourced from the Yelp website"],"prefix":"10.7717","member":"4443","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,4,30]],"date-time":"2024-04-30T04:34:19Z","timestamp":1714451659000},"score":37.18863,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/peerj.com\/articles\/cs-2011\/supp-1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7717\/peerj-cs.2011\/supp-1","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.2011","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,5]],"date-time":"2026-05-05T13:53:17Z","timestamp":1777989197892,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"PeerJ","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.3772\/fig-4","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,17]],"date-time":"2026-04-17T08:15:22Z","timestamp":1776413722000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Figure 4: The mean index for the sentiment classification on IMDb dataset."],"prefix":"10.7717","member":"4443","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,17]],"date-time":"2026-04-17T08:15:22Z","timestamp":1776413722000},"score":36.82797,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/peerj.com\/articles\/cs-3772\/fig-4"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7717\/peerj-cs.3772\/fig-4","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.3772","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,13]],"date-time":"2026-04-13T11:05:02Z","timestamp":1776078302535,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"EWA Publishing","issue":"1","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["ACE"],"abstract":"<jats:p>Sentiment analysis has become crucial for understanding consumer behavior in e-commerce and social media. While models based on transformers like Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers (BERT) and A Robustly Optimized BERT Pretraining Approach (RoBERTa) have great performance in Natural Language Processing (NLP) tasks, challenges persist in domain-specific language nuances and context sensitivity. This study addresses these gaps by utilizing DeBERTa, an advanced model with disentangled attention mechanisms, to improve sentiment classification. The methodology involves fine-tuning the DeBERTa-base on the IMDb dataset and evaluating its generalization on the Amazon Polarity dataset. The results achieved 93.21% accuracy, 91.28% precision, 94.98% recall, and 93.32% F1 score, achieving a good balance between precision and recall while maintaining high accuracy. The result of this study demonstrates that Decoding-enhanced BERT with Disentangled Attention (DeBERTa) has strong performance in handling long, structured text and short, diverse comments. This illustrates DeBERTa's superiority in capturing complex semantic relationships and context-dependent sentiments.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.54254\/2755-2721\/2025.kl22625","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,6]],"date-time":"2025-05-06T05:23:23Z","timestamp":1746509003000},"page":"198-201","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Enhancing Sentiment Analysis with Fine-Tuned DeBERTa in a Cross-Domain Study on IMDb and Amazon Polarity Datasets"],"prefix":"10.54254","volume":"149","author":[{"given":"Zijian","family":"Cao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Dundee International Institute, Central South University, Changsha, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"32523","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,6]]},"container-title":["Applied and Computational Engineering"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,13]],"date-time":"2026-04-13T10:15:11Z","timestamp":1776075311000},"score":36.67162,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ace.ewapub.com\/article\/view\/22625"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,6]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,22]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.54254\/2755-2721\/2025.kl22625","ISSN":["2755-2721","2755-273X"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2755-2721","type":"print"},{"value":"2755-273X","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,6]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,28]],"date-time":"2026-02-28T09:31:29Z","t